  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "戲劇、影視與文化",
    "sub_ename": "DRAMA, FILM & TELEVISION AND CULTURE",
    "describe_ch": "戲劇為綜合藝術，結合劇本、音樂、表演、美術設計等領域而成。本課程三大主題：戲劇概說、戲劇經典一（古典）、戲劇經典二（當代）。首先瞭解戲劇定義，並對當代影視採用的戲劇元素，進行反思與討論。具備基礎知識後，安排古典、當代兩部戲劇經典為授課主軸：古典劇作可為當代借鏡、當代劇作呼應傳統經典，皆反映多元社會文化風貌。透過主題式閱讀經典劇作、欣賞影視表演、選取專題報告與討論，藉此訓練鑑賞審美、思辨論述之能力。",
    "describe_eh": "Drama is an integrated art that combines fields of script, music, performance, art design, and so on. Three major themes of this course: Introduction to Drama, Drama Classics I (Classical), Drama Classics II (Contemporary). First, to understand the definition of drama, and introspect and discuss the drama elements used in contemporary film and television. After students acquire the basic knowledge, two classical and contemporary drama classics are arranged as the main focus of teaching. Classical dramas can be borrowed for contemporary times, while contemporary dramas echo traditional classics. Both reflect the diverse social and cultural features. Through thematic reading of classic plays, appreciation of film and television performances, and selection of special reports and discussions, students will have the ability to appreciate aesthetics and think critically is trained.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
